        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Christopher Buckley, William F. Buckley Jr., Patricia Buckley\n- Organizations: National Review\n- Products: Firing Line\n- Topics: conservative movement, newspaper columns, spy novels\n\nFacts:\n- William F. Buckley Jr. founded National Review magazine in 1955.\n- National Review had a major impact in stimulating the conservative movement.\n- William F. Buckley Jr. hosted 1,429 episodes of the television show Firing Line from 1966 to 1999.\n- William F. Buckley Jr. became known on Firing Line for his transatlantic accent and wide vocabulary.\n- William F. Buckley Jr. wrote a nationally syndicated newspaper column and numerous spy novels.\n- Christopher Buckley is the son of writer William F. Buckley Jr. and socialite Patricia Buckley.",
